---
import LessonLayout from '../../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
---
<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Our Vocation to Beatitude" cic="CCC 1716-1729" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
  <li>What did St. Augustine say about the human heart's desire for happiness?</li>
  <li>How many beatitudes are there and where are they found?</li>
  <li>What does each beatitude promise?</li>
  <li>What does it mean that the beatitudes are the &laquo;portrait of Christ&raquo;?</li>
  <li>What is the eternal beatitude that awaits us?</li>
</ol>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What has been the happiest moment of your life? What made it so special?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Does it relate to God, love, service?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. In what &laquo;worldly&raquo; things have you placed your hope for happiness? Have they disappointed you?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Money, recognition, relationship, health&hellip;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Which beatitude do you find hardest to live? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Examine your heart honestly. Which beatitude feels countercultural to you?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Is there someone in your life who seems to live the beatitudes? What impresses you about them?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. Which beatitude do you commit to living this week? How will you do it concretely?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Write your own beatitude</h4>
<p>Imagine Jesus looking at you today and saying: &laquo;Blessed are you...&raquo; What would he say? Write your personal beatitude based on your current situation.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Meditate on one beatitude each day</h4>
<p>This week, each day choose a different beatitude. When you wake up, read the beatitude of the day and ask yourself: &laquo;How can I live this today?&raquo; At the end of the day, write briefly how you lived it.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. The portrait of happiness</h4>
<p>Find an image (photo, painting, drawing) that for you represents true happiness. Paste it here or describe it. Then ask yourself: does it have anything to do with the beatitudes?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;Blessed are the pure in heart, for they shall see God.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Matthew 5:8</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord Jesus, you who taught us the way of happiness,<br />
help me to trust in your beatitudes.<br />
When the world tells me that happiness is in having,<br />
remind me that it is in giving.<br />
When it tells me it is in power,<br />
remind me that it is in serving.<br />
When it tells me it is in pleasure,<br />
remind me that it is in loving.<br />
Make me poor in spirit, meek, merciful,<br />
pure in heart, and a builder of peace.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>
</section>

<section class="content">

<hr />

<div class="downloads">
<a href="javascript:window.print()" class="download-btn">Print Workbook</a>
</div>
</section>

</LessonLayout>
